---
// /datasets — Dataset Register (wording-kanon.md "Catalogues": die zweite der beiden
// maschinell gepflegten Nachschlagewerke, NICHT "Dataset Hub" — "hub" ist gesperrt, das
// bezeichnet die Startseite der Ökologie).
//
// Stand 2026-07-27: zurückgebaut auf Null (docs/design/2026-07-27-register-rueckbau-und-
// scouts.md, Franks Entscheidung). Diese Seite zeigt deshalb einen leeren Bestand — und
// sagt, warum, statt so zu tun, als sei nur noch nichts gefunden worden. Die
// Aktualitäts-Regel (CLAUDE.md) verlangt genau das: überholte Strukturen werden sichtbar
// und datiert archiviert, nie unauffällig als aktuell stehen gelassen.
//
// Auskunft-vor-Poesie (wording-kanon.md "Prinzipien"): zuerst "was ist das hier?", dann
// der Befund, dann der Bestand.
//
// Zur Kanon-Regel "Zahlen nur aus Daten rendern": Die laufende Zahl kommt aus ENTRIES.
// Die Zahlen im Rückbau-Abschnitt beschreiben einen VERGANGENEN, datierten Stand — sie
// sind Protokoll, keine Live-Angabe, und als solches gestempelt. Sie dürfen hier fest
// stehen, weil sie sich nie wieder ändern können; ein veralteter Live-Wert wäre eine
// Lüge, ein datierter Vergangenheitswert ist ein Beleg.
import { ENTRIES } from '@/lib/register'

const total = ENTRIES.length
const RUECKBAU_DATUM = '2026-07-27'
---

<main id="main" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:py-14">
  <header class="mb-10">
    <p class="mb-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-fg-faint">Dataset Register</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Dataset Register</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted">
      A curated record of datasets that this ecology's research has actually reached for.
      Every entry carries the source's literal access route, how far that route has been
      checked, and — this is the part that matters — one sentence saying why the entry
      counts for the work going on here.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
      It is deliberately small. An entry cannot exist without its reason, and a reason
      cannot be generated from a keyword. That constraint is the whole design.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- Der Befund. Datiert, weil er ein Ereignis ist und kein Zustand. -->
  <section class="mb-10 rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel p-6">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-fg-faint">
      Reset · {RUECKBAU_DATUM}
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-fg">The register was rolled back to zero</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      Until this date the register held 16,516 entries, harvested by running a keyword
      sieve over 56,620,404 DataCite records, and published 8,590 pages. It was rolled
      back to nothing — not trimmed, not re-filtered — because the method underneath it
      measured the wrong thing.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      A keyword in a title usually names a <em>role</em>, not a <em>subject</em>.
      “Training data for MaxQuant” means these proteomics measurements trained a model —
      not that the dataset is about AI. The same trap sits under “neural network”,
      “surveillance”, “census”. A sieve counts word occurrences and reports it as
      relevance.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      What settled it was a count rather than an opinion. Of the 16,507 DOIs in the
      register and the 89 DOIs the three practices had ever cited in their own research,
      the overlap was <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">zero</strong>. Part of that
      gap is structural — the practices mostly cite papers, the register held datasets —
      but the conclusion survives it: this holding had never once served the research it
      was built for.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      Nothing measured was destroyed. The harvest, the rejection log with its reasons, the
      source windows and the failure notes all remain in the
      <a
        href="https://github.com/frankbueltge/dataset-hub"
        class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:text-fg"
        rel="noopener">dataset-hub</a> repository, where they are a quarry to be worked,
      not a record to be displayed. What ended is the claim that those 16,516 entries were
      relevant — a claim nobody had ever checked, one entry at a time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Der Bestand. Bei 0 sagt die Seite, dass 0 der ehrliche Stand ist. -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line pb-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-fg">Holdings</h2>
      <div class="text-right">
        <span class="font-mono text-2xl font-semibold tabular-nums text-fg">{total}</span>
        <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-fg-faint">
          entries
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {total === 0 ? (
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
        Empty, and that is the accurate state — not a source outage, not a failed build.
        The register is being grown again from the other direction: instead of collecting
        what exists and hoping something useful is in it, it will collect from the
        research outwards.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4">
        {ENTRIES.map((e) => (
          <li class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel p-4">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">{e.title}</h3>
              {e.verify_status === 'toVerify' && (
                <span
                  class="shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint"
                  title="admitted by the scout, not yet read over by hand">?</span>
              )}
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{e.relevance}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint">
              <a href={e.access_url} class="hover:text-fg" rel="noopener">{e.identifier}</a>
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    )}
  </section>

  <!-- Was kommt. Als Vorhaben markiert, nicht als bestehende Fläche. -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="border-b border-line pb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-fg">What comes next</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      Nightly scouts will read what the three practices are actually working on and search
      outwards from there — for datasets, which land here, and for papers, which get a
      catalogue of their own. What they find is an extension of the material the practices
      run into anyway, not a parallel collection beside it.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      Anything a scout admits is marked as unread until someone has gone over it, and the
      version history is the way back. This surface stays at zero until there is something
      here that earned its place.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
